22:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Reap incomplete multipart uploads."}]," When a multipart upload fails mid-flight\nthe store issues ",["$","code",null,{"children":"AbortMultipartUpload"}]," to clean up, and OCI honors both\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"ListMultipartUploads"}]," and ",["$","code",null,{"children":"AbortMultipartUpload"}],". A process killed ",["$","em",null,{"children":"before"}]," it\ncan abort still leaves orphaned parts, which is what the lifecycle rule is for."]}]
23:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Status."}]," This backend lives under ",["$","code",null,{"children":"experimental_cloud_object_store"}],". When it\nwas added, its core paths (read, write, existence checks, ranged reads,\nmultipart and integrity) were verified against live OCI, including an\nend-to-end Bazel remote cache round trip, a 2 GiB multipart upload of roughly 400 parts with full byte\nverification, multipart abort and cleanup, and 200-way concurrent load. It has\nnot been benchmarked at sustained production scale or duration."]}]
